         text="After Zama, Carthage accepts Scipio's peace: it keeps its African lands but gives up its elephants and all but ten warships, and pays 10,000 talents over fifty years. Livy says Scipio had about 500 ships towed out to sea and burned, and the sight struck the citizens like the burning of the city itself.",
