         text="Cato the Elder, sent to arbitrate between Carthage and Numidia, is alarmed by the city's wealth. Back in the Senate he lets fall a fresh fig from Carthage, picked three days before, and ends every speech with his demand that Carthage be destroyed. The famous phrase 'Carthago delenda est' is a later wording.",
